}}

==Enemy==
This single-target enemy has high speed and rapid attacks for an early-game threat, as with many pushers in Empire of Cats.

==Strategy==
When first encountered, Jackie Peng can be rather difficult to defeat since he has decent health, attack power and strikes quickly. Use his single-target attacks to your advantage and block him out with a steady line of [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]], while using [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] to deal fair damage to him. If you're unable to stall him, try gaining [[Treasure]]s to activate the [[Energy Drink]] and upgrade Tank Cat as well as Research. Any [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attacker]] would be helpful if he comes in swarms, like in [[Ghana (Empire of Cats)|Ghana/Wakayama]].

After [[Dubai (Empire of Cats)|Dubai/Hiroshima]], a squad of [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] should be able to hold him off until the [[Cat Cannon]] or another stronger unit finishes him. Another simple way of dealing with Jackie Peng would be to use fast-attacking cats and defensive cats, for example, [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cats]] coupled with Wall Cats.

Later on, Jackie Peng is just a minor threat or even free money as he can be easily taken out by most attackers.

